<title>USA: St Joseph hogs off $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs off $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 lower. Top $49.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Everybody decided to sell hogs at the same time, unbelievable 128,000 Interior Iowa movement Wednesday. Packers broke the market yesterday after several days of sharp price advances. Nice weather and producers busy applying chemicals and getting corn ground ready to plant but decided to come to market before hogs dropped back down below 50.00 again.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    48.50-49.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    47.00-48.00</p>
<p>    US 2-4	290-310 lbs    45.00-46.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady/off $2.00. Top $49.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2	300-450 lbs    45.00</p>
<p>		    450-500 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3	500-550 lbs    47.00</p>
<p>		    550-700 lbs    48.00-49.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	300-700 lbs    40.50</p>
<p>		    200-300 lbs    41.50</p>
</text>
